\section{System Architecture and Methodology}
\label{sec:methodology}

TERRA (Temporal-Evolution and Reasoning-Trace RAG) is designed as a two-phase, closed-loop GraphRAG architecture for high-stakes legal temporal reasoning. The core engineering philosophy strictly separates offline corpus ingestion and knowledge structure construction from online query routing and inference. This separation ensures that all computationally intensive graph traversals, citation link extractions, and reasoning trace generations are performed offline, maintaining responsive online inference with a bimodal latency profile (median \TerraFastPathMedianSeconds~s on factual lookups vs. \TerraHardPathMedianSeconds~s on multi-hop citation chains).


